# 6. Values sent back to the slide

In this example, the control points of a curve are dragged with the mouse. The curve is either a Bezier
curve, which approaches its points, or a Catmull-Rom spline, which goes through them. The program computes the
length of the curve, and the slide displays it while the points are moved: the value goes from the demo to the
slide.

